<title-group><article-title>Colchicine after lacunar stroke</article-title></title-group>
<abstract><p>We tested colchicine <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1">1</xref>.</p></abstract></article-meta></front>
<body>
<sec id="s1"><title>Introduction</title>
<p>Colchicine lowers recurrent stroke risk after lacunar infarction. [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r1">1</xref>, <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r2">2</xref>] Earlier trials (e.g. in Fig. 1 of a review) were small [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r3">3</xref>]. No citation here.</p>
</sec>
<sec id="s2"><title>Results</title>
<sec><title>Imaging</title>
<p>Infarct volume fell by 30% with colchicine (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1A</xref>). Edema was unchanged <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="r4">4</xref>.</p>
